session:pr434Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "IncrementalReasoner (#83) already handled ABox (base-fact) retraction correctly via a backward-forward DRed-style algorithm, but had no equivalent for TBox (axiom/rule) retraction -- removing an OWL axiom required a full from-scratch rebuild of the reasoner. The issue explicitly asked to verify, not assume, whether Derivation already tracked which rule produced each fact before building retraction logic on top of it. Checked datalog/src/types.rs and reasoner.rs directly: Derivation::rule_id already existed and was already populated on every record() call, so no new provenance tracking was needed -- the only new state added was DatalogProgram::disabled_rules (a HashSet<usize>), since rules can never be physically removed from the rules Vec without shifting indices and corrupting every other rule's existing Derivation::rule_id references. Landed three new APIs: owl_ontology::Ontology::remove_axiom (drops a value-equal axiom from the model), owl2rl2datalog::axiom2datalog (the existing private per-axiom translator made pub, used directly rather than going through owl2datalog's whole-ontology dedup/reorder), and IncrementalReasoner::apply_rule_deletions (takes Rule values rather than an invented RuleId type, to avoid leaking DatalogProgram's internal per-stratum indexing across the crate boundary), which resolves each rule to its derivation-record occurrences, runs a backward phase seeded from derivation.rule_id matches instead of deleted base facts, then re-derives via the same forward-phase and FALLBACK_THRESHOLD full-rematerialisation shape as the existing apply_deletions." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:434 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr434Decision ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr434 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

session:pr434Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "apply_rule_deletions' public signature takes &[Rule] (compiled Datalog rule values), not a RuleId/index type, even though internally each rule is resolved to a (program_index, rule_id) position for the backward-phase seed. Also documented as a precondition (not enforced by the type system) that the caller must have already computed the set difference against the remaining ontology's owl2datalog(...) output before calling, since owl2datalog dedups its rule output -- two distinct axioms can compile to byte-identical Rule values, so a bare Rule alone can't reveal whether it's genuinely dead or still backed by a surviving axiom." ;
    agp:alternative "Introducing a dedicated RuleId newtype wrapping DatalogProgram's internal (program_index, rule_id) pair, and/or having apply_rule_deletions itself recompute the live rule set from a passed-in Ontology to detect still-live duplicates automatically. Rejected: a RuleId type would leak DatalogProgram's own per-stratum indexing scheme across the datalog/owl2rl2datalog crate boundary for no benefit the caller couldn't get from a plain Rule value; auto-detecting liveness would require IncrementalReasoner to hold a reference to the whole Ontology it may not have (it's constructed from a bare rule list today), a bigger API surface change than this issue's scope justified." .
